      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow is a neutral third party, like the escrow agent, who holds funds and documents securely during the real estate transaction. These funds are held temporarily to ensure both the buyer and seller fulfill all their contractual obligations. Essentially, the escrow agent acts as a trusted intermediary, releasing the money to the appropriate party only when all agreed-upon conditions, like inspections and title checks, have been met.",
