    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. so basically they are just a middleman. is it weird though that we have to send our actual money to some random company instead of just giving it to the seller or something? feels kinda risky to just have it sitting there in a separate account.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it might feel unusual, using an escrow agent actually insulates both parties from risk. Handing money directly to the seller before closing puts all the risk on you if things fall apart later. The escrow account is legally protected and structured so that the funds aren't accessible until the final closing conditions are satisfied by all parties. This structure is designed precisely to protect your investment while money is changing hands.",
      "source": "target",
